"children":"Thumb pivots, 16th-note ghost notes, and why timing jitter destroys both funk pockets and control loops."}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-12","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-12 items-start","children":[["$","aside",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-3 lg:sticky lg:top-24 space-y-8 font-mono text-xs border-b lg:border-b-0 lg:border-r border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 pb-8 lg:pb-0 pr-0 lg:pr-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[10px] text-accent font-bold uppercase tracking-widest","children":"CHAPTER OUTLINE"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2 text-ink-dark/80 dark:text-paper-200/80 text-[11px]","children":[["$","li","the-percussive-bone",{"className":"hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#the-percussive-bone","className":"block leading-snug","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-mono mr-1.5","children":["0",1,"."]}],"I. The Percussive Bone"]}]}],["$","li","ghost-notes-as-state-machines",{"className":"hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#ghost-notes-as-state-machines","className":"block leading-snug","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-mono mr-1.5","children":["0",2,"."]}],"II. Ghost Notes as State Machines"]}]}],["$","li","phase-coherence-in-grooves-and-loops",{"className":"hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#phase-coherence-in-grooves-and-loops","className":"block leading-snug","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-mono mr-1.5","children":["0",3,"."]}],"III. Phase Coherence in Grooves and Loops"]}]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-2 pt-4 border-t border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 text-[10px] text-ink-muted","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":["AUTHOR: ","Matthew Chen"," (","陳軍宇",")"]}],["$","div",null,{"children":["LOCATION: ","Jiuru / Tamsui, Taiwan"]}],["$","div",null,{"children":["MOOD: ",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold uppercase","children":"Rhythmic"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"pt-2","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/Ch3nOff","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","className":"underline hover:text-accent","children":"GitHub @Ch3nOff"}]}]]}]]}],["$","main",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-6 space-y-12","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"drop-cap font-sans text-lg sm:text-xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-100 leading-relaxed font-light","children":"Most people view playing an instrument as an emotional endeavor. To me, slapping a bass guitar feels nearly identical to writing a low-level interrupt handler. If your hand lingers on the string for even three milliseconds too long, the harmonic is choked. If your thumb strikes at an angle off by five degrees, the percussive transient dissolves into muddy flub."}],[["$","section","0",{"id":"the-percussive-bone","className":"space-y-6 pt-4 scroll-mt-28","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 tracking-tight border-b border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 pb-2","children":"I. The Percussive Bone"}],"$undefined",[["$","p","0",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"Watch Marcus Miller or Victor Wooten closely. Their thumbs don't muscle through the string; they treat the knuckle like a spring-loaded hammer. You don't push into the instrument — you whip against it, bouncing off the steel so that the string's kinetic amplitude is transferred cleanly into the pickup magnets."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"In control systems, we call this critical damping. An underdamped thumb rings uncontrollably, creating unwanted sympathetic resonance on the adjacent D and G strings. An overdamped thumb suffocates the attack."}]],["$","figure",null,{"className":"my-8 py-6 border-y-2 border-accent/40 px-4 sm:px-6 bg-accent/5 dark:bg-accent/10","children":["$","blockquote",null,{"className":"font-serif italic text-xl sm:text-2xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 leading-snug","children":["“","Funk does not live in the notes you strike; it lives in the surgical precision of the silence you leave behind.","”"]}]}],"$undefined","$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:hidden p-3 bg-accent/5 border-l-2 border-accent font-hand text-accent text-sm","children":["Note: ","The instrument never lies about kinetic sloppy posture."]}]]}],["$","section","1",{"id":"ghost-notes-as-state-machines","className":"space-y-6 pt-4 scroll-mt-28","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 tracking-tight border-b border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 pb-2","children":"II. Ghost Notes as State Machines"}],"$undefined",[["$","p","0",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"The heart of a legitimate funk groove is never the downbeat root note. It is the muted 'chuck' — the ghost note. Left fingers rest loosely on the fretboard without pressing to the wood, while the right hand plucks."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"In a state machine, ghost notes are clock cycles where state does not mutate, but synchronization is maintained. Without them, the groove drifts. The listener feels anxious without understanding why: the system has accumulated micro-jitter."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}],["$","section","2",{"id":"phase-coherence-in-grooves-and-loops","className":"space-y-6 pt-4 scroll-mt-28","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 tracking-tight border-b border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 pb-2","children":"III. Phase Coherence in Grooves and Loops"}],"$undefined",[["$","p","0",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"When I wrote the feedback loop for my dual-loop PID library, I noticed the exact same mathematical phenomenon. If the differential term kicks in 2 milliseconds late relative to the velocity error, the robotic actuator stutters."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"Whether you are aligning a stepper motor's PWM duty cycle or locking in with an acoustic drummer at 112 BPM, phase coherence is the only thing standing between pure musical momentum and catastrophic oscillation."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:hidden p-3 bg-accent/5 border-l-2 border-accent font-hand text-accent text-sm","children":["Note: ","Music and robotics are just two dialects of applied physics."]}]]}]],["$","footer",null,{"className":"pt-12 border-t border-ink-dark/20 dark:border-paper-100/20 space-y-4 font-mono text-xs","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[10px] text-accent uppercase tracking-widest font-bold","children":"[FOOTNOTES & FORMAL CITATIONS]"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-2 list-decimal list-inside text-ink-muted text-[11px]","children":[["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-100 font-sans","children":"A roundwound steel string against a jumbo nickel-silver fret produces a transient spike in the 2.5kHz - 4kHz range within 1.2 milliseconds of impact."}]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-100 font-sans","children":"Ghost notes (dead notes) contain almost no pitch fundamental, acting strictly as rhythmic impulse markers."}]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"hidden lg:block lg:col-span-3 space-y-8 font-mono text-xs border-l border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 pl-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[10px] text-accent font-bold uppercase tracking-widest block","children":"MARGINALIA & NOTES"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"p-3 bg-paper-100/50 dark:bg-paper-900/50 border border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 space-y-1 relative","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[8px] text-accent uppercase tracking-widest block","children":["ANNOTATION § 0",1]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"margin-hand text-base text-accent","children":["“","The instrument never lies about kinetic sloppy posture.","”"]}]]}],null,["$","div","2",{"className":"p-3 bg-paper-100/50 dark:bg-paper-900/50 border border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 space-y-1 relative","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[8px] text-accent uppercase tracking-widest block","children":["ANNOTATION § 0",3]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"margin-hand text-base text-accent","children":["“","Music and robotics are just two dialects of applied physics.","”"]}]]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"p-4 border border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 bg-paper-100/30 text-[10px] space-y-2","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-accent uppercase font-bold tracking-widest","children":"PERSONAL DISCIPLINE"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-sans text-ink-dark/80 dark:text-paper-200/80 leading-normal","children":"All code samples and algorithmic theorems are tested on real silicon before archiving."}]]}]]}]]}]}]]}],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L4",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","article","children","$5","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L6",null,{}],"templateS